-- rules/inquiry/ontology.rofl — the inquiry kernel's EDB contract and ledgers.
-- Perspective discipline: docs/choosing-perspectives.md. Kind taxonomy:
-- docs/inquiry-kinds.md. This file holds facts only; rules live in
-- epistemic.rofl / obligations.rofl / intents.rofl.
--
-- EDB asserted by the framer (default [main], the shared working book):
--   inquiry(Id, Kind)            -- Kind: decide|verify|explain|explore|design|monitor
--   requires(Id, Claim)          -- proof obligation of the inquiry
--   blocking(Id, Claim)          -- blocking obligation (implies requires)
--   claim(C)                     -- the claim exists in the frame
--   observable(C)                -- some experiment/scan could verify it
--   ambiguous(C)                 -- the claim's meaning is not settled
--   requires_authority(C)        -- only a human authority can settle it
--
-- EDB asserted into the observation journal [obs] by the runtime only:
--   supports[obs](Evidence, Claim)
--   refutes[obs](Evidence, Claim)
--   evidence_kind[obs](Evidence, Kind)   -- measured|human_assertion|agent_claim
--
-- Ledgers:
--   [obs]        source ledger, sole writer: runtime (evidence journal)
--   [epistemic]  derived ledger, sole writers: the rules in epistemic.rofl
--   [main]       shared working book: frame EDB + obligation/intent derivations

-- only the runtime may write the observation journal; an agent asserting
-- into [obs] surfaces as forged[audit] with no further enforcement code.
authority(obs, runtime).

-- the working book reads the epistemic ledger wholesale (explicit knowledge
-- flow; rules writing INTO [epistemic] auto-bridge via their explicit heads).
imports(main, epistemic).
